      "content": "While you're a healthy individual, the risk of infection is higher with a puncture wound from a rusty object. Scrubbing and applying ointment can help prevent infection, but considering the potential for infection and the wound coming from a rusty object, it's still recommended to visit the doctor. The doctor can assess the wound, provide guidance, and assess your vaccination status to ensure you're up-to-date on any necessary boosters. Waiting 45 minutes isn't ideal if there's a risk of infection.",
